            <ArticleTitle>An algorithm for the evaluation and treatment of sacroiliac joint dysfunction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>445-9, 451</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Approximately 90 percent of adults experience an episode of low back pain in their lifetime. Sacroiliac joint (SIJ) dysfunction has been shown to cause approximately 13-30 percent of LBP in the adult population. SIJ fusion is becoming an increasingly popular treatment alternative for SIJ dysfunction. This paper presents a literature-based algorithm to assist the clinician in the evaluation and treatment of patients with suspected SIJ dysfunction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
